messages[14]{user,text}:
  user_2,[00:00] Hello, am I speaking with Neha Chauhan?
  user_1,[00:05] Yeah, hi. Neha here. Who is this?
  user_2,[00:09] Hi Neha, this is Karan Joshi calling from Safe Step Insurance, partnering with DCoders. I'm following up on our recent email and chat regarding your health policy renewal.
  user_1,[00:19] [sighs] Oh right. Look, I told the other person on chat already—I'm not renewing it.
  user_2,[00:27] Ah, I understand, ma'am. I just wanted to double-check if there was any particular issue? We noticed the grace period for your policy payment actually ended a few days ago, so--
  user_1,[00:39] Look, Karan, it's nothing personal, but I switched companies last month and my new employer provides a comprehensive group health cover. I literally have no use for this individual plan anymore.
  user_2,[00:52] Understood completely. That makes total sense if you've got corporate coverage now. I just need to officially process this as expired in our system since the payment window lapsed without renewal.
  user_1,[01:06] Yeah, fine by me. Do I need to fill out any forms or sign anything, or does it just drop off?
  user_2,[01:14] Um, no paperwork needed on your end. Since the deadline passed and you're opting out, I'll just update the status in our portal to 'Expired' right now. [typing sounds]
  user_1,[01:28] Perfect. Will I get some kind of confirmation email or anything? Just so I have it for my records.
  user_2,[01:35] Yes, absolutely. Once I hit save here, the system will automatically dispatch a closure notice confirming that policy number DC-HLT-9921 has officially expired.
  user_1,[01:48] Awesome. Thanks for making it quick and not giving me a hard sales pitch. [laughs slightly]
  user_2,[01:54] Haha, no problem at all, Neha. We don't like wasting your time. Is there anything else regarding your account I can help clear up today?
  user_1,[02:04] Nope, that's everything. Thanks, Karan. Have a good day.
  user_2,[02:08] You too, Neha. Take care! Bye.